Aim:
To draw lines, rectangles and rounded rectangles using Java Applet.

Algorithm:
1. Import the AWT and Applet packages.
2. Create a class named linerect that extends Applet.
3. Use the paint() method.
4. Draw lines using drawLine().
5. Draw rectangles using drawRect() and fillRect().
6. Draw rounded rectangles using drawRoundRect() and fillRoundRect().

Program:
import java.awt.*;
import java.io.*;
import java.applet.*;

/* <applet code="linerect.class" height=300 width=300>
</applet> */

public class linerect extends Applet {
    public void paint(Graphics g) {
        g.drawLine(10,10,50,50);
        g.drawRect(10,60,40,30);
        g.fillRect(60,10,30,80);
        g.drawRoundRect(10,100,80,50,10,10);
        g.fillRoundRect(20,110,60,30,5,5);
        g.drawLine(100,10,230,140);
        g.drawLine(100,140,230,10);
    }
}

Output:
Lines, an outlined rectangle, a filled rectangle, rounded rectangles and crossing lines are displayed.

Result:
Thus, lines and rectangles were drawn successfully using Java Applet.
